{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "API, Application Program Interface"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Application Program Interfaces."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understand important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.   Exchange simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives to Talk  About Tools for Web Design and Software Using More"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <b>comparatives</b> to show the differences between two or more objects, persons or things."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Long Adjectives</strong></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "An adjective with more than two syllables is a <b>long adjective</b>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p><strong>LONG ADJECTIVES</strong></p><strong>3- more syllables</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li>Interesting</li> <li>Difficult</li> <li>Important</li> <li>Expensive</li> <li>Intelligent</li> <li>Dangerous</li> <li>Sophisticated</li> </ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make comparisons with <b>long adjectives</b> you must use \u201c<i>more</i>\u201d before the adjective, and the conjunction \u201c<i>than</i>\u201d after the adjective. Check the structure that we use:  </br></br><center> Subject + verb + more + adjective + <b>than</b> + complement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: </br><i>This application is <b>more interesting than</b> its previous version. </br>Some programs can be <b>more difficult</b> to run <b>than</b> others."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's why API for windows is more important than other applications. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, MFC is more functional than Win32 because it works with the programming language C++, which is an object-oriented language with generic features. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, we could say that MFC is more explicit than Win32."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Useful Tech Terms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The terminology that was once merely a part of the technology field is nowadays everywhere. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here you can find some modern expressions related to technology; in fact, some of them are used in daily life contexts. And, others just make reference to essential computing terms."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"MORE TECH TERMS\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>1. Huge pipes</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This is the informal expression to say that an Internet connection has a goodly bandwidth.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>2.&nbsp;Mommy-save</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Colloquial expression to indicate that someone clicks on the bottom \u201csave\u201d without knowing which folder to save in. Its particular name is due to moms which sometimes don't understand so much about technology and feel confused when performing a task in a computer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>3.&nbsp;Multitasking</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When a computer can run many programs at the same time, it is considered to perform multitasking. This expression is also used in daily life when a person is able to do different activities at the same time. This evidences humans trying to be as computers.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>4.&nbsp;Photoshopped</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It comes from the word <i>photoshop</i>, which is a graphic program that lets you modify images. When something is <i>photoshopped</i>, it means that it was touched up before.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>5.&nbsp;Plug-and-play</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When a person buys a modern computer, he does not have to worry about drivers or installing programs as these computers are plug-and-play. That means that as soon as you plug in any additional device to the computer, it is ready to work. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interact "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to work with other parts at the same time and in a collaborative way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These applications let the computer systems interact with different programs, like in a multitasking process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disk file "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a magnetic file containing data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, reading information stored in disk files, sending commands to the printer, or displaying diagrams and text lines on the monitor are cases in which we can appreciate API. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "call upon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to request something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The programmer doesn't have to design everything because he can call upon a software library with different services ready to use."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dialog box  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a way to show information, to warn or to ask for permissions in a computer system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sure, an API call should consist in calling to a particular function, such as a dialog box."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "generic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a programming paradigm that consists in giving parameters based on algorithms  to operate "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, MFC is more functional than Win32 because it works with the programming language C++, which is an object-oriented language with generic features."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "imperative "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a programming paradigm that consists in giving commands to a program to operate "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: On the contrary, Win32 works with the programming language C, which is a language with imperative features."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find someone who uses API for his/her job and ask about the importance of this resource. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a descriptive text where you explain the importance of API."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find someone who uses API for his/her job and I ask about the importance of this resource.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a descriptive text where I explain the importance of API."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n4le01ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: Good morning class! Today we're going to talk about API. So, Joshua, how much do you know about it?</br>\n<strong>Joshua</b></strong>: Excuse me, Mrs. Lawrence, but I don't remember that topic.</br>\n<b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: Don't worry! API refers to Application Program Interfaces. These applications let the computer systems interact with different programs, like in a multitasking process. For example, reading information stored in disk files, sending commands to the printer, or displaying diagrams and text lines on the monitor are cases in which we can appreciate API. </br>\n<b>Joshua</b>: Now, I remember, an API makes a program more functional since the programmer doesn't have to design everything because he can call upon a software library with different services ready to use.</br>\n<b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: Exactly! That's known as an API call.</br>"}, {"time": "57500", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Joshua</b>: Could you explain us more about that, please?</br>\n<b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: Sure, an API call should consist in calling to a particular function, such as a dialog box. Then, the system answers with a pointer, known also as a handle, indicating that the application access is permitted, in this case the dialog box.</br>\n<b>Joshua</b>:  What happens with higher operating systems like Windows?</br>\n<b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: In that case, the API must count with a larger operating system. It is more sophisticated than other operating systems as it has to contain more functions, data and definitions.</br>\n<b>Joshua</b>: I see. That's why API for windows is more important than other applications. </br>"}, {"time": "107000", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Mrs. Lawrence</b>: Yes! To finish, you must know that there are different interfaces related to software design. Some of them are MFC (Microsoft Foundation Classes) and Win32. Both are programming libraries; however, MFC is more functional than Win32 because it works with the programming language C++, which is an object-oriented language with generic features. On the contrary, Win32 works with the programming language C, which is a language with imperative features. </br>\n<b>Joshua</b>: So, we could say that MFC is more explicit than Win32.</br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n4le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}